BND-15: do not let the evaporation adjustment make the rate negative

setEvap() added the monthly [ADJUSTMENTS] EVAPORATION value to the source
rate with no lower bound. An adjustment more negative than the source rate
(e.g. -0.10 in/day on a 0.05 in/day month) gave a negative Evap.rate, and
getSubareaRunoff() then booked negative evaporation that added water to
ponded and depression storage. Stop the adjusted rate at zero. Non-negative
rates are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-15_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/climate.c b/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
index c343b93..58ae8a5 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
@@ -1262,8 +1262,8 @@ void setEvap(DateTime theDate)
         Evap.rate = 0.0;
     }
 
-    // --- apply climate change adjustment
-    Evap.rate += Adjust.evap[mon - 1];
+    // --- apply climate change adjustment (the rate cannot go below 0)
+    Evap.rate = MAX(0.0, Evap.rate + Adjust.evap[mon - 1]);
 
     // --- an API prescribed evaporation rate overrides the data-source
     //     value (applied after adjustments so the prescription is final;
